<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρον-ίων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>son of Cronos</i>, i.e. <u>Zeus</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.397
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς Κρονίων</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				502
			</span></i>, al.: gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονίονος</span> only
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.247
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.620
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονιών</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), name of a month at Samos, etc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				976.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, al. [<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονίων, Κρονίονος</span>, in other cases
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span>: but <i><span class="en">
				Tyrt.
				2.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.23
			</span></i>, etc., use <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> in
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονίων</span>.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
